WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:02.160
- At the beginning of the war,

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.080
the US were very reluctant about

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.470
what they were prepared to give Ukraine.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.450
Now we're at a point where
they're talking about

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:11.040
sending F-16s.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.750
How have you moved their position?

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.063
How have you persuaded
them to come on board.

00:00:15.972 --> 00:00:20.305
(Yermak Speaks in foreign language)

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.790
- On a recent visit to Kyiv,

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.650
I sat down with Andriy Yermak,

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.750
the chief of staff and closest advisor

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:51.390
to Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky.

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.610
He's the point person
for talks with the West

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:56.550
on weapons, sanctions and much more.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:58.080
We talked about how the country

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.880
defied expectations in the war,

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.925
and what they've done to
maintain the support of the West.

00:01:02.925 --> 00:01:07.258
(Yermak speaks in foreign language)

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.620
- The US election takes place next year.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:39.570
Do you feel under any pressure

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.190
to bring the war to a close

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:45.030
before the possibility of a
second Trump administration

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:48.356
given his views on helping Ukraine?

00:01:48.356 --> 00:01:52.689
(Yermak speaks in foreign language)

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:56.400
- In the weeks prior to Russia's

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.110
full-scale invasion of Ukraine,

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:01.590
Mr. Yermak represented
Kyiv in talks with Moscow.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:03.870
Now, he says that as
long as Russia's troops

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:07.590
remain in Ukraine, direct
negotiations aren't possible.

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:09.480
You tried to negotiate

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:12.300
some sort of truce or deal before the war,

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:13.560
and that obviously didn't work,

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.330
what lessons have you learned from that

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:18.869
about how you deal with the Russians?

00:03:18.869 --> 00:03:23.202
(Yermak speaks in foreign language)

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:07.410
- Towards the end of our conversation,

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:10.260
Mr. Yermak reflected on
the solidarity for Ukraine

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:11.790
that he and President Zelensky

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:13.650
have worked to amass around the world

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:14.790
and why for him,

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:17.400
this war transcends
geographical boundaries

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.295
and has become a war about values.

00:04:20.295 --> 00:04:24.628
(Yermak speaks in foreign language)

